  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Three forces act on a block which is sliding down a slope at constant speed. <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"W\"></span> is the weight, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span> is the reaction force at the surface of the block and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span> is the friction force acting on the block.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>In this situation</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">there must be an unbalanced force down the plane.</li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"W=R\"></span>.</li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F=W\"></span>.</li><li data-label=\"D\">the resultant force on the block is zero.</li></ol>"
  },
